g to come together to make sure that  stacey abrams doesn't win this race and  that we keep georgia moving in the right  direction you know unlike her brett i  believe georgia is the greatest state in  the country to live work and raise our  families and i'm proud we're the number  one state in the country for business  and that's what i'm working to keep well  she was asked about that statement  here's her response to that  i think it was an artfully delivered  my point was a point that i've made many  times there may have been a a phrasing  that i could have done better but my  intention and my re and the reality is  true and that is brian kemp doesn't care  about certain communities in the state  and she went on to defend that saying uh  going right to  the issue of guns and saying that your  record on guns in georgia is going to be  a big part of this election  what do you think about what she said  and that issue in your election upcoming  well she's trying to mask over what the  real issues are in the state of georgia  which is 40-year high abiding inflation  she criticized us sending a billion  dollars back to the taxpayers instead of  wastefully spending it to help them  fight prices at the grocery store we  suspended the gas tax for over two  months to help lower the price at the  pump to help offset disastrous domestic  energy policies she criticized that she  wants to raise taxes uh you know she she  doesn't you know she she and her party  they want to defund the police well in  georgia we've been standing with law  enforcement and we've been going after  violent criminals but we also have just  passed the mental health parity act and  a lot of other things to address issues  that we have in our state and that's  what i'm looking forward to campaigning  on is my record because i have one and  the record that she has is that she  thinks she knows better what georgians  should be doing in the government than  our own citizens and that's what i'm  fighting a